<article class="env-proposition" id="048D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048D">Proposition <span data-tag="048D">5.4.1.7</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For every pair of objects $X,Y \in \calC $, the space $\bHom _{\calC }(X,Y)$ is essentially small. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every small collection $S$ of objects of $\calC $, the full subcategory of $\calC $ spanned by the elements of $S$ is essentially small. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from criterion $(1)$ in Propositions <a href="/tag/5109" data-tag="5109">5.4.1.2</a> and <a href="/tag/58E1" data-tag="58E1">5.4.1.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>